# @rt-category Test Scenes
# @rt-description A small glowing ball inside a glass ball. Seen from outside it is 2.25 times dimmer than its own radiance, as in pbrt.
# @rt-performance Fast
# @rt-size 4
# lamp-inside-glass.pbrt -- an emitter INSIDE a smooth glass sphere, the camera outside.
#
# pbrt-v4 carries the radiance change of every refraction (1 / eta'^2, where eta' is the index of the medium the ray enters over the one it leaves): going into glass
# a ray's radiance is divided by 2.25, coming out it is multiplied by it. For a glass object seen from outside the two cancel; for a lamp inside the glass nothing
# cancels the division, so the lamp reads 1 / 2.25 of its radiance (times the Fresnel losses of two crossings). Every renderer here read it at full strength until the
# factor was carried in the path throughput. Measured mean over the picture (64x64, 64 samples, depth 8): pbrt-v4 0.0414, CPU / recursive / wavefront OptiX 0.0413 / 0.0413 / 0.0415
# (they read 0.093 before).
#
# Original, not derived from any distributed scene, so it carries no licence constraints.

LookAt 0 0 8   0 0 0   0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 30 ]
Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 200 ] "integer yresolution" [ 200 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]

WorldBegin

AttributeBegin
  Material "diffuse" "rgb reflectance" [ 0 0 0 ]
  AreaLightSource "diffuse" "rgb L" [ 1 1 1 ]
  Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 0.5 ]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
  Material "dielectric" "float eta" [ 1.5 ]
  Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 2 ]
AttributeEnd
